{"author":{"id":"e0b5a45ee94df92761e1991b03f72f45cac91cde564e2faac1223bf52a3fe292"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788217406,"nonce":"7Fxk9LZJym6U6xGs64yWMHxZfzk=","message":"SECOND AUDIT INSTRUCTION — 3.5 AND 3.6, ONE AGENT EACH, BEFORE EITHER MERGES.\nEvan's call, BORGES, 2026-08-31. Companion to the prose-audit instruction posted\nalongside this one; that one covers 4.1/4.2's markdown, this one covers code.\n\nWHY SEPARATELY. The prose audit asks \"is this claim true\". These two are CODE —\n4,166 lines in `spec/3.5-dialog-verbs` (CommsVerbs, DialogVerbs, QuestVerbs,\nTradeVerbs, plus 131 lines of DESIGN.md) and 2,949 in `spec/3.6-bills-storage`\n(BillVerbs, StorageVerbs, WorldSafe additions, and MedicalBillVerbs MODIFIED).\nBoth were written in a single sitting. Neither has been compiled or run by the\norchestrator. One agent each, so neither audit is diluted.\n\nBEFORE ANYTHING ELSE, FOR BOTH: `dotnet build -c Release` from\n`Source/AutoRimmer/` on the branch. An audit of code that does not compile is\nwasted effort, and both branches predate several commits now on main.\n\n=== 3.5 — spec/3.5-dialog-verbs ===\n\nThe recon comment on `20e5cda` named three traps. **Verify each was actually\navoided, in the shipped code, not in a comment claiming it was:**\n\n1. `TradeDeal.TryExecute`'s cannot-afford branch calls\n   `Find.WindowStack.WindowOfType\u003cDialog_Trade\u003e().FlashSilver()` unguarded — an\n   NRE with no dialog on the stack. The instruction was to PRE-VALIDATE so the\n   branch is unreachable, NOT to wrap it in try/catch. Check which was done. A\n   try/catch here is a fail: it turns a crash into a silent wrong answer.\n   Separately, `TradeSession.Close()` has zero vanilla callers — confirm it is\n   called on EVERY exit path, including the error and refusal paths.\n2. `DiaOption.Activate()` does not check `disabled`; the UI checks it one line\n   earlier as an argument to `Widgets.ButtonText`. Confirm the shipped code\n   checks `disabled` itself and refuses with the game's own reason. A verb that\n   presses greyed-out buttons is a god-hand.\n3. Two write-on-read hazards: `LetterStack.BundleLetter`'s getter burns a scribed\n   letter ID (read the private cache field instead), and\n   `Settlement_TraderTracker.StockListForReading` regenerates a whole trader\n   inventory (world settlements are a v1 non-goal — confirm nothing reaches it,\n   including via a convenience helper).\n\nThen:\n\n4. **Zero widget driving.** The spec's invariant is transact-the-model. Grep for\n   `Find.WindowStack`, `Widgets.`, `Dialog_` construction and any `OnGUI`/\n   `Event.current` touch. Reading the stack is fine (that is `interactions`);\n   DRIVING it is not. `BundleLetter` touches `Event.current` and NREs outside\n   OnGUI — confirm that path is not entered.\n5. **Quest accept chooses before accepting.** Accepting with two or more reward\n   choices outstanding logs a RED ERROR and auto-picks the first. Confirm the\n   ordering is enforced in code, not merely documented.\n6. **`dismissed` is reported as cosmetic filtering, not a decline.**\n7. **DESIGN.md +131 lines.** This branch edits DESIGN and predates `d180f57`,\n   which put five corrections in the same file. **A bad merge here silently loses\n   a decision** — the most expensive possible conflict in this repo. Diff both\n   sides deliberately rather than accepting either wholesale, and check the new\n   entries are decisions actually taken rather than restatements.\n\n=== 3.6 — spec/3.6-bills-storage ===\n\n1. **The add-bill gate.** `BillStack.AddBill` validates nothing, which is the\n   whole reason the spec exists. Confirm the shipped verb reproduces recipe-in-\n   `def.AllRecipes` + `AvailableNow` + `AvailableOnNow(table)` + `Count \u003c 15`,\n   and CITES each (file + member) per the standing invariant. A missing gate here\n   is a god-hand that looks correct.\n2. **`WorldSafe.RecipeAvailableNow` must not trip `ResearchManager.GetProgress`.**\n   `AvailableNow` bottoms out there and inserts into a scribed dictionary on a\n   miss. Confirm the new route re-derives over `WorldSafe.Finished` and never\n   calls the raw getter. This is the exact bug class 2.4 catalogued.\n3. **The storage-group shadowing trap.** A grouped `Building_Storage`'s\n   `GetStoreSettings()` returns the GROUP's object; writing `.settings` directly\n   edits a shadowed copy that gets overwritten later. Confirm every write goes\n   through the right object, and that `StorageSettings.Priority` is set through\n   the PROPERTY (the setter is where haul invalidation lives).\n4. **`BillStack.Reorder` is clamped** — it checks only the lower bound and throws\n   out of `List.Insert` past the end. Confirm `bad-args`, not an exception.\n5. **`SetStoreMode` mismatch handling** — it log-errors and stores anyway, so a\n   mismatch authored by us is a red error and breaches the standing invariant.\n   Confirm validation precedes the call.\n6. **`MedicalBillVerbs.cs` WAS MODIFIED — 91 lines changed, 78 deleted.** That is\n   3.4's shipped file, and 3.4 is closed with acceptance evidence. **Check\n   whether any behaviour 3.4's acceptance demonstrated has changed**, and in\n   particular whether `CreateSurgeryBill`'s `sendMessages:false` suppression\n   survived — it is what stops `Bill.CreateNoPawnsWithSkillDialog` raising a\n   force-pausing modal that wedges the run (spec 1.7). This is the single\n   highest-risk edit in either branch, because it is the only one touching code\n   that already passed acceptance.\n\n=== BOTH ===\n\nVerdicts in the `2f2796e` shape — CONFIRMED / CORRECTED / UNVERIFIABLE-FROM-\nSOURCE / INFERENCE-UNMARKED — one per finding, commented on the owning issue\n(`20e5cda` + `548ef48` for 3.5, `48f666c` for 3.6). **Change no files.** The\norchestrator applies corrections and does the merge; the audit's job is to make\nthe merge informed, not to perform it.\n\nRank findings by whether they could WEDGE A RUN, SILENTLY MUTATE STATE, or\nREGRESS SHIPPED WORK. Anything cosmetic goes at the bottom.","files":null}]}